## F2 withdrawn: the color format check

- The earlier item said the writer color check was weaker than the Workbooks checkColor.
- Workbooks checkColor (dashboard/lib/storytime/print/picture-check.ts:238-250, read-only)
  requires PNG format, no alpha, no 4 channels, exactly 3 channels, and space srgb or rgb.
- The writer inspectColorPrint at d06690a0 refuses a palette PNG, a depth other than uchar,
  a bitsPerSample other than 8, a space other than srgb, and a channel count other than 3. It
  keeps the PNG format, pixel size, and no-alpha checks.
- The writer covers every Workbooks rule and adds the palette refusal. It accepts only srgb.
  sharp reports srgb for an 8-bit RGB PNG, so the Muse flow sees no false refusal.
- Test T171 covers the palette, one-channel, 16-bit, and four-channel refusals.
- F2 is closed. Withdrawn.

